  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Cli\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Cli\n       Program: commons-cli\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/Cli.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-cli.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 39\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Cli-13\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n538fb6889f0387a40b821cfb315685e929110736\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-06-09 07:37:19 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCLI-61\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CLI-61\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.BugLoopingOptionLookAlikeTest::testLoopingOptionLookAlike2\n   --> junit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<Unexpected [testfile.txt while processing ]> but was:<Unexpected [value \"testfile.txt\" found while processing  input]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.WriteableCommandLine\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.commandline.WriteableCommandLineImpl\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.option.ArgumentImpl\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: [cli] argument defaults prevent commandline usage.\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nI have found a bug in the following scenario:\n\nYou have an option which can take a single argument which in turn has a default\nvalue. You supply a value on the command line which is intended to override\nthis default however as the CommandLine already has a value for this Option,\nthis second value is not allowed and the command line cannot be parsed.\n\nI have created a patch which adds a method to WritableCommandLine and its Impl\nwhich allows you to retrieve the undefaulted values for an Option. I have then\nchanged ArgumentImpl to use this method to determine the argument count\n\nComments:\n\n[Andrew Shirley]: Created an attachment (id=18121)\nA patch for this issue\n\na patch which adds a method to WritableCommandLine and its Impl which allows\nyou to retrieve the undefaulted values for an Option. A change to ArgumentImpl\nto use this method to determine the argument count\n\n[Andrew Shirley]: Created an attachment (id=18122)\nA test for this issue\n\nThree tests which verify expected behaviour on this issue\n\n[Brian Egge]: I tested this patch out, and it makes sense.  It's the same issue as CLI-145, and the solution is better than the patch I created.  I would apply this patch, and then apply the test case from CLI-145.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Applying Andrew's fix on top of Brian's fix to CLI-145. Rolling back the addition of getMessageKey to OptionException.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.cli2.WriteableCommandLine (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli2.WriteableCommandLine (fixed)\n@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@\n      * @param option the Option associated with the values\n      * @return a list of values or an empty List if none are found\n      */\n+    List getUndefaultedValues(final Option option);\n \n     /**\n      * Sets the default values for an Option in the CommandLine\n\n--- org.apache.commons.cli2.commandline.WriteableCommandLineImpl (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli2.commandline.WriteableCommandLineImpl (fixed)\n@@ -129,9 +129,17 @@\n         return valueList;\n     }\n \n+    public List getUndefaultedValues(Option option) {\n       // First grab the command line values\n+      List valueList = (List) values.get(option);\n \n       // Finally use an empty list\n+      if (valueList == null) {\n+        valueList = Collections.EMPTY_LIST;\n+      }\n+\n+      return valueList;\n+    }\n \n     public Boolean getSwitch(final Option option,\n                              final Boolean defaultValue) {\n\n--- org.apache.commons.cli2.option.ArgumentImpl (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli2.option.ArgumentImpl (fixed)\n@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@\n                               final Option option)\n         throws OptionException {\n         // count of arguments processed for this option.\n-        int argumentCount = 0;\n+        int argumentCount = commandLine.getUndefaultedValues(option).size();\n \n         while (arguments.hasNext() && (argumentCount < maximum)) {\n             final String allValuesQuoted = (String) arguments.next();"
}